<!--
  Sitemap for qulaycafe.uz.

  Only the five URLs the apex really serves are listed. The landing hostname
  answers *every* unmatched path with the marketing page (see server.ts), so a
  crawler that guesses paths can invent unlimited URLs that all return 200 —
  the canonical tag on each document and this explicit list are what tell
  Google which ones are real.

  The app surfaces are deliberately absent: clients. pages need a restaurant
  and table from a QR code, and admin./kitchen. are behind a login. There is
  nothing there for a crawler to index.

  lastmod is hand-maintained. Update it when the page's copy actually changes;
  a date that moves on every deploy teaches Google to ignore the field.
-->
